{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["And he said: Where is their Elohim — and the nations too will say: Where, pray, is the Elohim of Israel? 'For the sake of My name's honor I will grant them deliverance and take vengeance on their enemies' — for already at first He said, אַפְאִיהֶם — upon Israel — וְהַשְׁבַּתִּי זֵכֶרָם — were it not for the fury of the enemy who boasts, saying: Our hand is exalted. But now, when the impoverishment and the trouble among the enemies of Israel grows so great that their power fails, and the idol-worshippers say: Our hand is exalted, and say: Where is their Elohim — therefore I will take vengeance on them, to sanctify My name which they profane."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:57.623633128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}